      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think it is safer not to clear all the registers that you clear here since the spec says they should be preserved, but that applies to all the other 32 bit calls as well.\n\nAgreed. The problem is that under FF-A 1.2, we cannot rely on the function ID of the call to tell 32 bit calls apart from 64 bit ones (FF-A 1.3 fixes that). We know that `FFA_VERSION` is a 32 bit call but the consensus that emerged from the upstream discussion around `ffa_set_version` was that when breaking the spec, we should at least do so consistently [0]. In the current version, we diverge from FF-A to the same degree on both arms of the conditional we\u0027re adding.\n\n[0] https://lore.kernel.org/all/aH-0cx9YhdWRe2nq@willie-the-truck/",
      "parentUuid": "8c6a8969_72b4c131",
      "revId": "b38a667ad73aae0beec2a67ee9617c247c7fede1",
